{"_id":"post-sample-hero-background-in-astro","_type":"post","title":"Add a shader hero background to an Astro site in 5 minutes","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"hero-background-in-astro"},"excerpt":"A walkthrough from npm install to a live Aurora hero, with content layered on top.","publishedAt":"2026-11-10T09:00:00Z","author":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"author-bedant"},"tags":[{"_type":"reference","_ref":"tag-tutorials","_key":"k00072"},{"_type":"reference","_ref":"tag-astro","_key":"k00073"}],"relatedComponents":[{"_type":"reference","_ref":"component-aurora","_key":"k00074"}],"body":[{"_key":"k00000","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00001","_type":"span","text":"A shader background is the quickest way to make a landing page feel alive. Here is the whole process in Astro, start to finish.","marks":[]}]},{"_key":"k00002","_type":"block","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00003","_type":"span","text":"Install","marks":[]}]},{"_key":"k00004","_type":"code","language":"bash","code":"pnpm add @shadermix/astro"},{"_key":"k00005","_type":"block","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00006","_type":"span","text":"Drop it into your hero","marks":[]}]},{"_key":"k00007","_type":"code","language":"astro","code":"---\nimport { Aurora } from '@shadermix/astro';\n---\n<section class=\"hero\">\n  <Aurora speed={0.5} />\n  <h1>Ship faster</h1>\n</section>"},{"_key":"k00008","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00009","_type":"span","text":"The effect fills its parent, so give the section a height and position: relative, and your text sits above it.","marks":[]}]},{"_key":"k00010","_type":"shadermixEmbed","effect":"aurora","options":"{\"speed\": 0.5}","height":280,"caption":"The result — a live Aurora behind hero copy."}]}
{"_id":"post-sample-webflow-without-code","_type":"post","title":"Shader backgrounds in Webflow, no code required","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"webflow-without-code"},"excerpt":"One script tag in Footer code and a custom attribute is all Webflow needs.","publishedAt":"2026-11-06T09:00:00Z","author":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"author-bedant"},"tags":[{"_type":"reference","_ref":"tag-tutorials","_key":"k00075"},{"_type":"reference","_ref":"tag-webflow","_key":"k00076"}],"relatedComponents":[{"_type":"reference","_ref":"component-mesh-gradient","_key":"k00077"}],"body":[{"_key":"k00011","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00012","_type":"span","text":"Webflow designers usually reach for Lottie or a looping video for animated backgrounds. Both are heavy. A shader is a few kilobytes.","marks":[]}]},{"_key":"k00013","_type":"block","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00014","_type":"span","text":"Step 1 — add the script","marks":[]}]},{"_key":"k00015","_type":"code","language":"html","code":"<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@shadermix/webflow\" defer></script>"},{"_key":"k00016","_type":"block","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00017","_type":"span","text":"Step 2 — set an attribute","marks":[]}]},{"_key":"k00018","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00019","_type":"span","text":"Select any Div Block, open Settings, and add a custom attribute named sm-effect with the value mesh-gradient.","marks":[]}]},{"_key":"k00020","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00021","_type":"span","text":"Tune it with more sm-* attributes, like sm-speed or sm-colors.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_key":"k00022","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00023","_type":"span","text":"It re-initialises automatically after CMS pagination.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_key":"k00024","_type":"shadermixEmbed","effect":"mesh-gradient","options":"{\"speed\": 0.3}","height":280,"caption":"mesh-gradient, configured entirely from attributes."}]}
{"_id":"post-sample-how-we-keep-effects-fast","_type":"post","title":"How Shadermix keeps WebGL effects fast","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"how-we-keep-effects-fast"},"excerpt":"One shared animation loop, paused when off-screen, capped pixel ratio, and a static frame for reduced motion.","publishedAt":"2026-10-30T09:00:00Z","author":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"author-bedant"},"tags":[{"_type":"reference","_ref":"tag-performance","_key":"k00078"}],"relatedComponents":[{"_type":"reference","_ref":"component-grain-gradient","_key":"k00079"}],"body":[{"_key":"k00025","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00026","_type":"span","text":"A beautiful background that drains a laptop battery is a bad background. Every effect follows the same performance rules.","marks":[]}]},{"_key":"k00027","_type":"block","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00028","_type":"span","text":"The rules","marks":[]}]},{"_key":"k00029","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00030","_type":"span","text":"A single requestAnimationFrame loop drives every effect on the page.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_key":"k00031","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00032","_type":"span","text":"Effects pause when scrolled out of view or when the tab is hidden.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_key":"k00033","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00034","_type":"span","text":"Device pixel ratio is capped at 2.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_key":"k00035","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00036","_type":"span","text":"prefers-reduced-motion renders one static frame.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_key":"k00037","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00038","_type":"span","text":"Lost WebGL contexts fall back to a CSS gradient.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_key":"k00039","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00040","_type":"span","text":"The result is that a page with three effects costs about the same as a page with one.","marks":[]}]}]}
{"_id":"post-sample-choosing-colours-for-gradients","_type":"post","title":"Choosing colours for animated gradients","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"choosing-colours-for-gradients"},"excerpt":"Why gradients look muddy, and how linear-space blending fixes it.","publishedAt":"2026-10-22T09:00:00Z","author":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"author-bedant"},"tags":[{"_type":"reference","_ref":"tag-tutorials","_key":"k00080"}],"relatedComponents":[{"_type":"reference","_ref":"component-mesh-gradient","_key":"k00081"},{"_type":"reference","_ref":"component-aurora","_key":"k00082"}],"body":[{"_key":"k00041","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00042","_type":"span","text":"If you have ever blended blue into yellow and got grey in the middle, you have met sRGB blending.","marks":[]}]},{"_key":"k00043","_type":"block","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00044","_type":"span","text":"Blend in linear space","marks":[]}]},{"_key":"k00045","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00046","_type":"span","text":"Shadermix converts every colour you pass to linear light before the shader mixes it, then back again for display. Midpoints stay vivid.","marks":[]}]},{"_key":"k00047","_type":"block","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00048","_type":"span","text":"Practical tips","marks":[]}]},{"_key":"k00049","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00050","_type":"span","text":"Pick two or three colours with similar brightness for calm backgrounds.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_key":"k00051","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00052","_type":"span","text":"Add one high-contrast accent for energy.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_key":"k00053","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00054","_type":"span","text":"Lower the speed before lowering saturation.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"number","level":1},{"_key":"k00055","_type":"shadermixEmbed","effect":"mesh-gradient","options":"{\"colors\": [\"#ff6b6b\", \"#4d96ff\", \"#ffd93d\", \"#6bcB77\"]}","height":280,"caption":"Four colours, blended in linear space."}]}
{"_id":"post-sample-roadmap-to-v1","_type":"post","title":"The road to Shadermix 1.0","slug":{"_type":"slug","current":"roadmap-to-v1"},"excerpt":"Ten effects at launch, then text effects, page blocks, and a Pro tier.","publishedAt":"2026-10-15T09:00:00Z","author":{"_type":"reference","_ref":"author-bedant"},"tags":[{"_type":"reference","_ref":"tag-announcements","_key":"k00083"}],"relatedComponents":[],"body":[{"_key":"k00056","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00057","_type":"span","text":"Here is what is planned between the first release and 1.0.","marks":[]}]},{"_key":"k00058","_type":"block","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00059","_type":"span","text":"v0.1 — launch","marks":[]}]},{"_key":"k00060","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00061","_type":"span","text":"Ten background effects for Astro, Webflow, and plain JavaScript.","marks":[]}]},{"_key":"k00062","_type":"block","style":"h2","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00063","_type":"span","text":"After launch","marks":[]}]},{"_key":"k00064","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00065","_type":"span","text":"Text effects and reveal animations.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_key":"k00066","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00067","_type":"span","text":"A CLI installer: npx shadermix add aurora.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_key":"k00068","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00069","_type":"span","text":"Shadermix Pro: page blocks and full landing-page templates.","marks":[]}],"listItem":"bullet","level":1},{"_key":"k00070","_type":"block","style":"normal","markDefs":[],"children":[{"_key":"k00071","_type":"span","text":"Everything in the core stays MIT-licensed and free.","marks":[]}]}]}
